A||N||20||bcwawright||Will Northstar bolt to Getrag||||5||
Z||000000||bcwawright||07-06-2001||08:51 PM||||I was going to buy a Northstar and want to know if the 5spd Getrag will bolt up without mods?? Also would like to know which Nstar works better in a Fiero...the OBDII or the preOBDII engine??<BR>Thanks<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Will||07-06-2001||09:28 PM||||The Northstar will not bolt to a getrag without mods to the Getrag case. The webbing inside the case must be cut away to clear the Northstar starter.<BR>Also one of the bell housing bolts may not line up correctly.<P>OBD I is easier, but either one will throw a fit, or at least a lot of codes, without the stock Automatic. I don't think any of the transmission codes will hamper engine operation, but I might be wrong.<BR>Worst case: engine won't or will barely run<BR>Best case: your SES light will be on constantly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||07-06-2001||09:30 PM||||from what I have heard. if it was obd2 you would use obd1 harness and sensors.  It should bolt to getrag, but the concern is that the n* is not designed to have a clutch force pushing in on crank shaft.  I believe you will also run into problems if you don't use the caddy electric trans (4t60e)   <P>BUT I am far from experienced in this area.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||07-06-2001||09:34 PM||||bolt up? allmost one bolt hole needs to be threaded backwards on it. but custom flywheel<BR>is needed look for CHRFAB on the net.<BR>pre obd2 throdle body and computer are said to work best newest motor is all forged inside and better than eary motors to rev higher or turbo or nox but computer is a nitemare  so look at a haltex box?<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-06-2001||09:35 PM||||also, your best bet would be to look into a 9 11/16" kevlar/kevlar or cindered iron clutch disk, as the Northstar puts out 275 ft-lbs of torque, unless you have a clutch in mind all ready that will withstand the torque.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||07-06-2001||10:07 PM||||SC3800 puts 273 ft-lbs to the wheels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||KRMFiero||07-06-2001||10:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PBJ:<BR><B>I believe you will also run into problems if you don't use the caddy electric trans (4t60e)   <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am pretty sure that they use the 4T80e for the Northstar, and the 4T60e for there lower powered engines <P>I could be wrong<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||07-06-2001||11:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PBJ:<BR><B>from what I have heard. if it was obd2 you would use obd1 harness and sensors.  It should bolt to getrag, but the concern is that the n* is not designed to have a clutch force pushing in on crank shaft.  I believe you will also run into problems if you don't use the caddy electric trans (4t60e)   <P>BUT I am far from experienced in this area.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think that crankshaft thrust from the clutch is a non-issue.<P>Can't the FieroShop put a N* bolt circle in one of their aluminum flywheels?<P>The N* puts out 295-300 ftlbs. I've talked with a guy at centerforce. He claims to have a Dual Friction clutch which will handle it and bolt to the stock V6 flywheel.<P>The larger pull type clutch from the 284 Getrag would be a B**** to adapt.<P>Phil:<BR>I have no doubt that with a low restriction exhaust and intake that the N* would put at least 275 ftlbs to the wheels.<BR>What mods do you have on your engine? Auto or manual transmission?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||West Coast Fiero||07-07-2001||12:03 AM||||Personaly, I would retain the 4T80-E from the caddy so as you would never worry about destroying a clutch, would you really want to take this thing apart again to install another clutch?||||reg||1
