Z||000012||artherd||07-07-2001||03:39 PM||||Hi there Bruce!, the Getrag will bolt up.<P>You have to notch part of the case to clear the in-vee starter motor.  (and possibly modify one bolt hole a bit to make it work, we will soon see :)<P>Use an aftermarket ECU from <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com." TARGET=_blank>www.chrfab.com.</A> <P>I am talking to them now about just how much they offer for the fiero (I belive they have a clutch and flywheel already.) These guys are way cool, and are building the next street rods. They even have hot cams, etc.<P>Why have a stick shift with a northstar?<BR>Persona preference. To me it's the same as asking "why drive a fiero?" I think it's a travestry they ever came with autos. (but hey, I think they should have all been 88 GT/Formulas with LT1s from the factory :")<P>300bhp from an engine which will weigh about 50lbs LESS than the 2.8.... over 200lb-ft available from about 1500rpm on... well...<BR>uh.... heh, that's pretty cool sounding to me :)<P><BR>Oh, and that's TOTAL BULL about the northstar's bearings, it was designed and built with eventual manual-transmission applications in mind, and thus can take the thrust of an unloaded pressure plate. (~1500-2000lbs) This is an established fact.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||Will||07-07-2001||03:43 PM||||Yes, the LMP Northstars use production block and bearings, and they're stickshift cars running in what has to be the most grueling on pavement race in the history of the universe.||||reg||1
Z||000014||bcwawright||07-08-2001||04:53 PM||||Hi artherd<BR>Thanks for the info.  Do you know of any aftermarket starters that can be installed to eliminate the need to cut the casting on the getrag??<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000015||Will||07-08-2001||11:46 PM||||I was finally able to get started fitting the transmission to the engine today.<P>The lower hole on the right does not line up. <P>The stock Northstar setup uses four bolts: lower left, upper two, lower right.<BR>The middle left hole does not exist because it is too close to the number 8 cylinder bore. The middle right hole is a dowel pin, but does not have any threads inside it.<P>For the lower right hole, three options exist:<BR>1) Use the hole in the engine (with a stud, probably), notch the edge of the transmission case, and mill a small clamping piece which will fit over the stud and clamp the transmission to the engine in that area.<BR>2) Use the hole in the transmission, notch the boss on the engine block, and do a similar clamping setup.<BR>3) possibly do both.<P>A small machining locating tab on the top of the bell housing must be removed to clear the coolant crossover manifold. This is easily doable with a hacksaw, and does not adversely affect the transmission, as the tab was only used to machine the case during production.<P>A minute amount of grinding must be done on the end of the throwout arm shaft to clear the coolant crossover manifold. I believe that all the other clutch and shift linkage components will fit without trouble, though I haven't mocked it up yet.<P>Any questions?||||reg||1
Z||000016||Andre||07-09-2001||01:32 AM||||Does anybody know if the late model Getrag from the Sunfire GT and Cavalier Z24 will bolt directly to the Northstar?  Does all 4 holes line up and what about starter interference?<P>------------------<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Andre (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jay||07-09-2001||09:57 PM||||I've converted my 1997 Northstar to a 1995 to bypass OBD2.  That included changing throttle body, TPS and O2 sensors.  As for codes, yes it does throw codes only on the highway.  The check engine light comes on and the car runs rich.  Dynoed it a few weeks back at 255hp to the wheels using the STS tranny.  No modifications to the engine, just dropped in.  I am running mid 13's all day long.  I'm also using a 1995 ECM with a 1994 Eprom.  Waiting on Chris for a reprogrammed chip.  Where is it? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Although I may have something else in developement from my end.<P>Jay <BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Mickey_Moose||07-09-2001||10:27 PM||||...well something else that would be interesting in the block from the Cyclone transplanted into the Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||MoneypitGT||07-09-2001||10:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Andre:<BR><B>Does anybody know if the late model Getrag from the Sunfire GT and Cavalier Z24 will bolt directly to the Northstar?  Does all 4 holes line up and what about starter interference?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Z24 and Sunfire GT use the Twin Cam/Q4 engine and are way different, so no.<BR>  Chris<BR><P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
